    "AI Notes": {
      "value": "German artist/photographer (b. 1968, Remscheid), works between Berlin and London. Defined 1990s visual culture with candid images of youth, nightlife and the LGBTQ community (early work for i-D); spans portraiture, still life, landscape and abstraction. First photographer, first non-British artist to win the Turner Prize (2000); major museum retrospectives (Tate Modern, MoMA). One of the most significant living artists, fully autonomous. Country Germany confirmed (added UK for his long London base). Photography tagged; as a Turner Prize artist, Art practice clearly applies too.",
